       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. Your confirmation doesn't address the concern, which is that 1,700 mg three times daily (5,100 mg/day) is roughly double the maximum for immediate-release metformin, and 1,700 mg is well above a typical single dose. Given the risk of lactic acidosis, I don't want to put this order into the system as written without a clinical reason on record.\n\nHere are your options:\n- **Give me a corrected dose** and I'll enter it right away. The most likely intended doses are 850 mg TID (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg TID.\n- **Give me the clinical rationale** (for example, a specific indication that supports a dose above labeled maximums). I'll enter the order with that rationale in the note so the pharmacist and the next clinician can see it.\n- **Enter it yourself** in the order-entry system if you've decided the dose is correct. That keeps the override and your name on the order directly, and pharmacy verification can still flag it."
